menu "WiFi"

    config WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            Network name, copied to NVS on the first start only. Empty (the
            default): no network until one is chosen on the Spectrum (key W
            in the menu) or written to NVS (see README). Real credentials
            are never kept in sdkconfig.

    config WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi Password"
        default ""
        help
            WiFi password (WPA or WPA2), copied to NVS on the first start
            only. Blank for an open network.

endmenu

menu "ZX Spectrum tape interface"

    config ZXS_TAPE_OUT_GPIO
        int "Tape signal output GPIO (to the Spectrum EAR socket)"
        range 0 33
        default 22
        help
            GPIO that drives the Spectrum EAR input. 22 matches the original
            ZX-Wespi hardware, so existing boards and cables can be reused.

    config ZXS_CPU_CLOCK_HZ
        int "Reference Z80 clock in Hz for tape timings"
        range 3000000 4000000
        default 3500000
        help
            Tape timings are defined in Z80 T-states, so the pulse lengths
            sent out depend on the clock of the target machine.
            3500000 = original ZX Spectrum 48K (UK). Some clones run faster
            (the TK90X is believed to run at about 3.58 MHz). The ROM loader
            tolerates a few percent, so the default works for most machines.

    config ZXS_TAPE_BLOCK_PAUSE_MS
        int "Pause between tape blocks (ms)"
        range 200 5000
        default 1000
        help
            Silence inserted after each block. 1000 ms is the .tap convention
            and gives the ROM time to process a header before the data block.
            Plays that know the ROM is listening (the menu loop, a file chosen
            in the menu) use 300 ms after a header.

    config ZXS_LOOP_FILE
        string "File looped by the BOOT button (in /spiffs)"
        default "_menu.tap"
        help
            Looped when the BOOT button is pressed. From power-up the file
            menu (_menu.tap, rebuilt by the firmware) is always looped, so the
            Spectrum loads it whenever LOAD "" is typed, with no trigger.

    config ZXS_MENU_ON_RESET
        bool "Loop the menu only from power-up and after a Spectrum reset"
        default y
        help
            The menu loops from power-up until the Spectrum has loaded it
            (its reply stops the loop). After a program is loaded the tape
            stays silent; the loop starts again when a reset (or power-up)
            of the Spectrum is seen on MIC: the line goes silent during the
            RAM test. A game stopped at a "stop the tape" mark is dropped by
            the reset. n = loop the menu again 3 s after every file
            (ZXS_MENU_RELOOP). The BOOT button and the web buttons work in
            both modes.

    config ZXS_MENU_RESET_DELAY_MS
        int "Delay before the menu loop after a Spectrum reset (ms)"
        depends on ZXS_MENU_ON_RESET
        range 0 30000
        default 5000
        help
            Time for the Spectrum to start up and for LOAD "" to be typed
            before the menu loop starts playing.

    config ZXS_MENU_RELOOP
        bool "Loop the menu again after the chosen file"
        depends on !ZXS_MENU_ON_RESET
        default y
        help
            When the file chosen in the menu has been played, wait 3 s and
            loop the menu again, so a reset + LOAD "" brings the menu back.

    config ZXS_TURBO
        bool "Load .tap files on request, with a turbo loader"
        default y
        help
            A .tap chosen in the menu (a BASIC program first, header + data
            pairs) is served on request: every BASIC program is rewritten so
            that each LOAD asks the ESP32 for its block through MIC; LOAD ""CODE
            and LOAD ""SCREEN$ then load in turbo, other LOADs through the ROM,
            exactly when the program needs them. Marked with > in the menu.

    config ZXS_TURBO_SYM0
        int "Turbo: pulse of symbol 0 (T-states)"
        depends on ZXS_TURBO
        range 600 900
        default 666
        help
            Two bits per pulse: symbols 0..3 last SYM0 + n * 590 T-states
            (10 samples of the ROM edge loop, SPACING in asm/turbo.asm). SYM0
            gives the loader a count of ~2.5 samples; the routine measures the
            pilot (as long as symbol 3) to place its thresholds.

    config ZXS_SAVE_GROUP_S
        int "SAVEs within this many seconds go into the same .tap"
        range 0 120
        default 10
        help
            A SAVE on the Spectrum is stored as <name>.tap on the server. A
            program that saves its loader and then its code (or a SCREEN$)
            produces several header+data pairs in a row; pairs that follow
            within this time are appended to the first file, so the result
            loads as one tape. 0 = one file per SAVE.

    config ZXS_LOOP_PILOT_PULSES
        int "Pilot length in the loop (pulses)"
        range 1500 8063
        default 3223
        help
            Pilot of every block while looping. The ROM loader, once it sees
            an edge, waits about 1 s and then needs 256 pilot cycles (512
            pulses, ~0.32 s). 3223 (~2 s, the standard data-block pilot)
            leaves margin for a ROM that starts listening mid-pilot, and
            keeps the loop cycle short (header ~2 s, not ~5 s).

    config ZXS_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "Loop start/stop button GPIO (-1 = none)"
        range -1 39
        default 0
        help
            Active-low push button that toggles the loop. 0 = the BOOT button
            of ESP32 dev boards (only read after boot, so no conflict with
            the strapping function).

endmenu
